Version 2.0.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* Incompatible changes:
  - The -s option is no longer the --cydia flag. It is now --server, and it
    needs a URL argument. The Cydia signature service no longer exists. A
    command line that used -s as a flag now reads the next argument as the
    URL. Remove -s from such command lines, or give it a URL.
  - The -p, --pwn option is only available if you build with limera1n
    support. This support is included by default. To leave it out, configure
    with --without-limera1n.
  - The build needs three new components: libimobiledevice-glue, libusbmuxd
    and libtatsu. The TSS code moved to libtatsu.
  - The build no longer needs OpenSSL or libuuid.
  - libplist must have JSON support.

* Minimum versions of the required components:

    Component                Version 2.0.0    Version 1.0.0
    ---------------------    -------------    -------------
    libimobiledevice         1.4.0            1.3.0
    libirecovery             1.3.1            1.0.0
    libplist                 2.7.0            2.2.0
    libusbmuxd               2.1.1            not required
    libimobiledevice-glue    1.3.2            not required
    libtatsu                 1.0.5            not required
    libzip                   1.0              0.8
    libcurl                  7.0              7.0
    OpenSSL                  not required     0.9.8

* New features:
  - Restore of iOS 15, iOS 16, iOS 17 and iOS 18 firmware files
  - Restore of macOS firmware files to Apple silicon Macs, up to macOS 27
  - Restore through DFU mode and Port DFU mode
  - Restore from RecoveryOS
  - Support for the iPhone 16 family, the iPhone 17 family baseband (Mav25)
    and Macs with an M4 chip
  - New --ipsw-info option, which prints the contents of a firmware file
  - New --variant option, which selects the build identity to use
  - New --logfile option, which writes the log output to a file
  - New --ignore-errors option, which continues the restore after some
    errors
  - New --exclusive-usb option on macOS. It keeps the deviceinterfaced
    daemon from taking the USB device during the restore. Use this option if
    the restore stops while it waits for the device to reconnect in DFU
    mode.
  - New --without-limera1n configure option, which builds without the
    limera1n exploit
  - Docker files, which make it easier to set up a build environment

Version 1.0.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* First official public release
* Features:
  - Restore firmware files to iOS devices
  - Use official IPSW firmware archive file or directory
  - Updates the device by default or allows full restore erasing all data
  - Download latest available firmware for device on demand
  - Cache downloaded firmware files
  - Restore using custom firmware files (requires bootrom exploit)
  - Skip NOR/Baseband upgrade
  - Fetch TSS records as ".shsh" files
  - Put devices in pwned DFU mode (limera1n devices only)
  - Use custom AP ticket from file
  - Developed since 2010
